once-example-typed
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: the operator's shape for the by-need example — typed Response,
  the ops named after the resources (Fetch.User/Plan/Feed) with smart
  constructors on the companion so the handler needs no type arguments
  and no ascriptions, and the row spelled `Response ! Fetch + Once`.
  Replaces the GetUser/String version in TestDirectOnce and in
  docs/direct-style.md. Also records what the literal first draft
  taught: `effect(Fetch.User(token))` with no expected type infers
  `Nothing ! Fetch`, losing both the answer and the row.
files: src/test/scala/TestDirectOnce.scala, docs/direct-style.md, CHANGELOG.md
